    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a difficult schedule today with the majority of our offensive core currently inactive, leaving **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero** to shoulder the load in marginal matchups. **Christian Yelich** earns the highest score of the day at 51.69, bolstered by a +13% dynamic platoon advantage against Rasmussen. While Rasmussen presents a respectable 3.30 xERA, the shift to the three-hole for **Christian Yelich** keeps his floor stable. **Junior Caminero** sits at a 49.84 efficiency score; his production is suppressed by the elite 2.35 xERA of Misiorowski, though he maintains value via the stability of the #3 spot in the order. We are essentially playing for high-contact outcomes here, as neither matchup offers the favorable environment necessary to push these scores into the \"Strong\" 60+ tier.\n\nOur bench strategy remains static due to team-wide off-days for core assets like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin**. Given that these high-leverage players are inactive, there were no difficult start/sit decisions today. Other depth pieces on our roster\u2014including **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Carson Benge**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014are also relegated to the pine due to the lack of schedule availability. We are currently in a holding pattern, looking to preserve our remaining game caps for when the rest of the roster returns to action. The primary risk today is the high-tier capability of Misiorowski; should **Junior Caminero** struggle early, we will be monitoring the late-game pinch-hit potential closely to ensure we don't bleed efficiency.",
